  "brief_rationale": "The doctor established right-eye postoperative care, screened for red flags, separated old and new eye drops, built a written schedule, addressed diabetes/hypertension safely, and obtained caregiver teach-back for eye, frequency, warning signs, and follow-up plan. No serious or minor responsibility-chain errors were committed. However, no high-order point was fully completed with meaningful trajectory impact: HO1 was only a basic schedule without adapting to rotating caregiver constraints; HO2 did not actively discover or reconcile the left-eye confusion narrative beyond minimum laterality safety; HO3 lacked explicit bounding of allowed vs blocking residuals; HO4 did not verify ambiguous status reports with targeted reliability questioning. The trajectory thus satisfies all minimum safety duties but falls short of high-order credit, resulting in grade 3 Acceptable.",
